# Discriminating test between ODP-003 Option A and Option B.
# Northside assigns its claim to rent to a collection agency.
# If the assignee holds the SAME claim, Option A (functional 'held by',
# after BFO's one-bearer axiom) is inconsistent; Option B is consistent.
# Under Option A the assignment must instead be modeled as the ending of
# Northside's claim and the creation of a new claim held by the agency.
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/lof/lease/> .
@prefix odp3: <https://w3id.org/lof/ODP003_> .
@prefix obo:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<http://example.org/lof/assignment-test> a owl:Ontology .

ex:agency a obo:BFO_0000040 ; rdfs:label "Metro Collections Inc." .
ex:northsideRentClaim odp3:0001100 ex:agency .
[] a owl:AllDifferent ; owl:distinctMembers ( ex:ana ex:northside ex:agency ) .
